    "specPath": "specs/033-provenance-rules-and-actionable-outcomes/spec.md",
    "status": "approved",
    "summary": "An amendment of approved specs 002 and 006, for #76 child B3. A definition may declare which provenance classes the caller controls, input checks whose consequence on failure depends on the provenance of the value tested (refuse, drop the field, relax a named constraint group, downgrade its grade, abstain, escalate, or continue with a notice), exhaustive over the classes the input accepts, and policy conditions over provenance. Every unresolved outcome, refusal and notice of such a plan carries who can act on it, a typed remediation, its causes with provenance, and whether retrying can succeed; who can act is computed from the causes, and an author may only move it away from the caller, never toward it. Adds the `needs_input` outcome with declared, literal questions and a continuation digest, and documents how hosts map outcomes to transport semantics. Adds to the #76 track versions `rustev.definition/2`, `rustev.plan/3` and `rustev.evidence/2`, and introduces `rustev.judgment/2`; plans using no construct of this spec keep their bytes and `PlanId`. Approved (A-30); implemented, with the Node binding's conformance item awaiting spec 027.\n",
    "title": "Provenance-conditional rules and actionable outcomes (amends 002 and 006)"
